From b547144921118fd3d844e29561ed0827fabc6cce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:57:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: qcom-pon: clear the reboot reason after boot

The reboot-mode driver writes PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE only for a known mode
(recovery, bootloader) and nothing for a plain reboot. The ZTE Axon 7's
bootloader does not clear the register either, so after one "reboot
recovery" every later plain reboot also went to recovery (seen on
LineageOS 24: 0x88f stayed 0x04). Downstream kernels write 0 on a normal
reboot. Clear the reason once the driver is up: the bootloader has used
it by then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i49UMoL3MhGT7nwMzG
---
 drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c b/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c
index 7e108982a..531390ef6 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c
@@ -78,6 +78,17 @@ static int qcom_pon_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			dev_err(&pdev->dev, "can't register reboot mode\n");
 			return error;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * The bootloader has acted on the reason by now. A reboot
+		 * without a mode writes nothing, so a stale "recovery" would
+		 * send every later plain reboot to recovery again (seen on the
+		 * ZTE Axon 7, whose bootloader does not clear it; downstream
+		 * kernels write 0 on a normal reboot). Clear it.
+		 */
+		regmap_update_bits(pon->regmap,
+				   pon->baseaddr + PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE,
+				   GENMASK(7, reason_shift), 0);
 	}
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, pon);
-- 
